# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Byte-for-byte checkout. DO NOT REMOVE.
#
# Every file here is hashed in MANIFEST.sha256 and that manifest is GPG-signed.
# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites LF to CRLF on
# checkout -- including MANIFEST.sha256 itself. The effect is total: every hash
# mismatches, and the manifest's own filenames acquire a trailing carriage return,
# so `sha256sum -c` reports "No such file or directory" for all of them.
#
# A verifier on Windows following our published instructions would see the entire
# archive fail to verify and reasonably conclude we are broken or lying. This line
# is what makes the archive checkable on every platform rather than only on Unix.
* -text

# This repository is a journalism / provenance DATASET, not a PHP application.
# The only code is the exporter + verifier tooling under scripts/; vendor it so
# GitHub Linguist stops classifying the repo as "PHP" and it reads as the
# markdown + JSON dataset it actually is.
scripts/** linguist-vendored
MANIFEST.sha256 linguist-generated
*.json linguist-language=JSON
